{:edb/db-before-t 2510 :edb/db-after-t 2511 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535823 50 #inst "2026-10-09T08:11:52.775Z" 13194139535823 true] [17592186119809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368360 13194139535823 true] [17592186119809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368367 13194139535823 true] [17592186119809 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368388 13194139535823 true] [17592186119810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368374 13194139535823 true] [17592186119810 1020 #edb/ref 17592186368381 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368361 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1089 "q-109712" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1100 "Find the surface area of the parametric surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y={v}^{2},\\,z=\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}\n$$\n\nfor $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}.$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1113 #uuid "8262518f-3842-5651-b1d9-5224332846b6" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368360 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\frac{2}{3}{v}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,2{v}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 2v & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-2{v}^{2},\\,2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2{v}^{2})^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{4}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{v}^{2}}=v$ since $v\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nNext, let's denote\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le \\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nThen, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{0}^{1}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}u\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the substitution \n\n$$\nw={v}^{2}+1\\,⇒\\,\\text{d}w=2v\\,\\text{d}v,\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{3}}2v\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}v \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{w}\\,\\text{d}w \\\\  & ={[\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{w}^{3}}]}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}[\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}] \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368362 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368363 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368364 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368365 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368366 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1041 "selection" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368364 13194139535823 true] [17592186368361 1110 #uuid "98403821-c63f-5312-bc66-d2288f3ae9e4" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368362 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368362 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368362 1111 #uuid "b3043c8e-4860-53bc-b1a6-e1ba31a60e98" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368363 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368363 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368363 1111 #uuid "19c49a1a-f217-551f-a8d3-1391bd5418d4" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368364 1034 "\\frac{14}{3}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368364 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368364 1111 #uuid "5b2450fb-1253-5afd-9c31-e9e5f1892df7" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368365 1034 "\\frac{19}{6}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368365 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368365 1111 #uuid "0de66c21-a952-5a1a-816b-9b5a223870ca" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368366 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368366 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368366 1111 #uuid "53657f4a-00fe-5925-af62-d0b432ad1e9a" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368368 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1089 "q-109779" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1100 "Find the surface area of the part of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-v⟩$ that is subject to the constraint ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9.$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1113 #uuid "815c0ebb-2900-5353-8633-596c7a148310" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368367 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-1,\\,1,\\,1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that the region ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9$ corresponds to the disk\n\n$$\nD={(u,v)\\,:\\,{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}\\le 9},\n$$\n\nof radius $3.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{∬}_{D}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\cdot (\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2}) \\\\  & =9\\pi \\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368369 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368370 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368371 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368372 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368373 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1041 "selection" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368372 13194139535823 true] [17592186368368 1110 #uuid "3147e495-7d19-5002-8291-82ed7f374d66" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368369 1034 "2\\sqrt{3}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368369 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368369 1111 #uuid "47ea83d0-43e8-5134-8b7b-bc6355bfbb89" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368370 1034 "\\pi \\sqrt{3}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368370 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368370 1111 #uuid "15eb8a3d-99ac-5d9d-b785-caebb6467dbc" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368371 1034 "9\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368371 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368371 1111 #uuid "93359eb9-e1fb-5a74-9793-f9fe879052d7" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368372 1034 "9\\pi \\sqrt{3}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368372 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368372 1111 #uuid "1b3960d8-7920-5e18-98ed-63fbbe8b2d8d" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368373 1034 "\\pi \\sqrt{2}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368373 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368373 1111 #uuid "a4ab9932-a696-50ea-ba06-0ca34c418293" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368375 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1089 "q-109947" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 1,\\,0\\le v\\le 1}\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨u+v,\\,3{u}^{2},\\,u-v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le 1.$ What is the missing expression?" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1113 #uuid "c235bda4-b647-59f5-b137-7fc5bc86576a" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368374 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,6u,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(3{u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 6u & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}6u & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6u \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-6u,\\,2,\\,-6u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6u)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-6u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{u}^{2}+4+36{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72{u}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4(18{u}^{2}+1)} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368376 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368377 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368378 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368379 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368380 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1041 "selection" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1104 #edb/ref 17592186368379 13194139535823 true] [17592186368375 1110 #uuid "cf7b55fd-b82e-5f75-822d-3acaf71a687e" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368376 1034 "\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368376 1111 #uuid "e16daed2-33c8-5909-b9c0-371e5e772c68" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368377 1034 "2u\\sqrt{9{u}^{2}+1}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368377 1111 #uuid "8d975feb-30c1-5948-97ec-435f2d64de14" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368378 1034 "2\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+1}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368378 1111 #uuid "0c6efc79-d2da-5ca1-b556-85a3d66178eb" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368379 1034 "2\\sqrt{18{u}^{2}+1}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368379 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368379 1111 #uuid "d027da9f-d814-5a71-a484-b43e9aeaedb2" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368380 1034 "u\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+4}" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368380 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535823 true] [17592186368380 1111 #uuid "ba916f02-4de2-5c79-b898-b64bc286ffce" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1017 #edb/ref 17592186368382 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1089 "q-110019" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1100 "$$\n{∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A,\\,D={(u,v)\\,:\\,0\\le u\\le 2,\\,0\\le v\\le \\pi }\n$$\n\nThe integral above gives the surface area of the parametric surface $r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1$ and $0\\le v\\le \\pi .$ What is the missing expression?" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1113 #uuid "8e92a306-a654-5aa7-ab29-bbc8c19240b4" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368381 1145 "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface area of $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & \\operatorname{cos}⁡v \\\\ 0 & -u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & 2u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u{sin}^{2}⁡v-2u{cos}^{2}⁡v,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨-2u,\\,2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2u)^{2}+(2{u}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v)^{2}+(4{u}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡v+16{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}({sin}^{2}⁡v+{cos}^{2}⁡v)+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+4{u}^{4}+12{u}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}(1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}}\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v} \\\\  & =2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $\\sqrt{{u}^{2}}=u$ since $u\\ge 0$ on $D.$\n\nTherefore, the surface area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2u\\sqrt{1+{u}^{2}+3{u}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}A\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535823 true] [17592186368382 1000 #edb/ref 17592186368383 1319